{"qid":"Q1541699","names":["County of Ampuria"],"title":"County of Ampuria","endonym":{"native":"Comtat d'Empúries","lang":"ca"},"capsule":"The County of Empúries (Comtat d'Empúries) was a Carolingian frontier county established around 812–813 in northeastern Catalonia, initially subordinate to the County of Girona and centred on the Gulf of Roses coast. Hugh I's dynasty maintained independent comital rule from 989; Pope Sylvester II confirmed its ecclesiastical boundaries in 1002, and one Empúrian fleet briefly seized the Balearic Islands. Hugh VI sold the county in 1325 to a son of King James II of Aragon, making it an apanage of the Crown of Aragon; it was formally annexed into the Principality of Catalonia in 1402, the title surviving thereafter as an honorific of the Dukes of Segorbe.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core comital territory is well attested from Carolingian and Aragonese charters; outer limits vis-à-vis Roussillon and Girona varied and are imprecisely reconstructed.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: County of Empúries","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Emp%C3%BAries"},{"label":"Britannica: Catalonia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Catalonia"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"County of Empúries","rulers":[{"qid":"Q2072026","name":"Hugh I, Count of Empúries","start":991,"end":1040,"image":null,"nativeName":"Hug I d'Empúries","nativeLang":"ca"},{"qid":"Q9061651","name":"Ponzio I di Empúries","start":1040,"end":1078,"image":null,"nativeName":"Ponç I","nativeLang":"ca"},{"qid":"Q4894977","name":"Hugh II, Count of Empúries","start":1078,"en